# Copy to `.env` at the repository root and fill in. That file is gitignored.
#
#   cp .env.example .env && chmod 600 .env
#   python -m qbs.agent --check
#
# `qbs.agent` reads this file on import, so the CLI, the dashboard and a
# notebook all pick it up with nothing further to do.
#
# A real environment variable ALWAYS wins over a line here, so
# `GOOGLE_API_KEY=... python -m qbs.agent ...` overrides the file for one run.
#
# Syntax is deliberately small: KEY=value, one per line, `#` starts a comment
# only at the beginning of a line, and a matching pair of surrounding quotes
# is stripped. No `$VAR` interpolation and no multi-line values -- export
# those from your shell instead.

# --- required for the LLM analyst ----------------------------------------
# https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# GEMINI_API_KEY is accepted too; Google's own docs use both names.
GOOGLE_API_KEY=

# --- the kill switch ------------------------------------------------------
# Set this to stop every Gemini call without uninstalling anything. Useful for
# capping spend, working offline, or ruling the model out while debugging.
# Everything that does not need it keeps working: picks, momentum profiles,
# breadth, fundamentals, search, and `python -m qbs.agent --report ...`.
#
# Only an explicit off-word re-enables it -- 0, false, no, off, none, disabled.
# ANY other non-empty value switches it OFF, so a half-remembered
# `QBS_DISABLE_ANALYST=disable` stops the spending rather than quietly
# leaving it running.
# QBS_DISABLE_ANALYST=1

# --- optional: two models, because they are not the same job ---------------
# The CHAT (Analyst tab) reasons over tool output turn after turn and re-sends
# its transcript each time -- measured at roughly 17x the news panel's usage.
# Cheap-per-token with thinking on is the right shape there.
# QBS_GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash
#
# Thinking budget for the CHAT only. -1 lets the model decide, 0 turns
# thinking off, a positive number caps it in tokens. The accepted range is
# model-specific; the API rejects a bad one rather than this file guessing.
# QBS_THINKING_BUDGET=-1
#
# The NEWS READ is one call a day over ~30 headlines -- about 73k tokens a
# month, pennies at any price -- so it gets the stronger model and no thinking
# budget, since it is extraction into a fixed JSON shape.
# QBS_SUMMARY_MODEL=gemini-2.5-pro
#
# To run ONE model for everything, set QBS_GEMINI_MODEL alone -- the summary
# follows it unless QBS_SUMMARY_MODEL is also set.
#
# Not sure a model name is real? `python -m qbs.agent --models` asks the API
# what this key can actually serve, rather than trusting any list.

# Better web search than the keyless DuckDuckGo default, and it costs money.
# Set this AND `pip install tavily-python`; qbs.agent.news then prefers it.
# TAVILY_API_KEY=

# Nothing else in this package needs a key. Prices come from Yahoo via
# yfinance, and the Interactive Brokers credentials for live trading live in
# deploy/docker/.env instead -- a different file, on the trading host only.
